## Security rules (non-negotiable)

{{ Pick the ones that apply. Delete the rest. }}

- Every API endpoint requires an auth dependency — no exceptions without a documented allowlist entry
- User input is never concatenated into SQL
- Secrets and tokens are never logged or returned in API responses
- File paths from user input are resolved and bounds-checked before reading

